# Lockfile. This repo is an umbrella workspace member: its cross-repo deps are
# `workspace:*` on packages that live in OTHER repositories (webrun-files), so
# `pnpm install` here can never resolve them — it fails with
# ERR_PNPM_WORKSPACE_PKG_NOT_FOUND. turbo.json likewise carries `extends: ["//"]`,
# a nested-config form only valid under the umbrella root. Both are deliberate.
# The authoritative lockfile is the umbrella's, which pins the whole cross-repo
# closure; the umbrella branch additionally records this repo's exact SHA as a
# gitlink. A lockfile here could not be regenerated, could not be used, and would
# only drift into saying false things about the dependency set.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# adversary-loop audit trails
.adversary-loop/
